## Closing answer

"A TrainRun is one train on one date with a route of stops; segment i runs from stop i to stop i+1, so a journey is a range of segments. Each Seat records which booking holds each segment, so the same seat can be sold Bengaluru–Jolarpettai to Asha and Jolarpettai–Chennai to Bilal. Booking finds seats free on every segment of the journey for every passenger; if there aren't enough, nothing is held and the booking joins a first-come waitlist. Cancelling releases that booking's segments and re-checks the waitlist in order. Booking and cancelling are atomic per train run – in a database, one conditional transaction on the seat-segment rows."
